  "prefLabel": "Env-Wr 303.07 Transfer of Ownership",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wr 303.07 Transfer of Ownership.\n\n(a) The owner shall provide the following information to any prospective owner prior to transferring:\n\n(1) Any and all deeds, easements, agreements, or other rights associated with the dam;\n\n(2) The state dam inventory number assigned by the department;\n\n(3) Any letters or orders issued by the department relative to the condition of the dam; and\n\n(4) The existing OMRF.\n\n(b) Within 30 days of the transfer of ownership of a dam or the property on which a dam is located, the new owner shall inform the department in writing of the transfer of ownership by providing the following:\n\n(1) The name of the former owner;\n\n(2) The state dam inventory number assigned by the department;\n\n(3) The name, mailing address, email address, and daytime telephone number of the new owner;\n\n(4) The tax map and lot number of the dam;\n\n(5) The volume and page number of the deed which transferred ownership of the dam or the property on which the dam is located;\n\n(6) An updated OMRF in accordance with Env-Wr 303.04, if the dam is classified as low, significant, or high hazard; and\n\n(7) An updated EAP, if one is required for the dam, in accordance with Env-Wr 500.\n\nSource. #1716, eff 2-20-81; ss by #2207, eff 12-13-82; ss by #2900, eff 11-7-84; amd by #4534, eff 11-30-88; rpld by #5080, eff 2-22-91\n\nNew. #8414, eff 8-20-05; ss by #10510, eff 1-22-14; ss by #13980, eff 5-24-24 (formerly Env-Wr 303.08)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wr100-900.html"
